rked with and we've placed them  in apprenticeships and they've gone on  to get great jobs many of those jobs by  the way if you just look at a job  posting they will say degree required  but it's actually not true employers  just want to know that you're gonna  create value for them and there are so  many ways that you can prove that better  than just that dead piece of paper one  of the things employers want is an  assurance that someone has vetted you  and that you're smart and that you kind  of  your act together the you have high  aptitude but also the capacity for  achievement without a degree how do you  convince some of that yeah you know it's  funny that you mentioned that a friend  of mine who is a CEO I just saw a tweet  of his recently he did a little poll and  he said this is not scientific but this  is a very much in line with the hundreds  of CEOs and hiring managers I've talked  with he said would you if you only knew  this about someone who would you rather  hire someone who'd run a marathon or  someone with a degree 85% said the  person who would run a marathon that's  just one example but that's one of those  things that you know it signals a lot of  things at once so look you can go out  and create projects and say hey I built  this I did this you can start offering  to do some projects do some work for  free you can go and build up kind of a  portfolio that showcases some of your  skills and interests figure out what are  you interested in build some actual  skills and start working on things and  if you just think about for a minute  zoom out if you were to enroll in  college in the fall three years from now  you'd still be in the classroom if  you're going to go and this fall and do  something like praxis or something where  you're going out you're getting some  work experience you're building a body  of work in three years you're gonna have  three years of professional experience  under your bank you're gonna have so  much more to leverage in